{"id":"mahabharata-6-054","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":54,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 54 · Third day: Duryodhana rebukes Bhishma","summary":{"en":"The Kaurava kings surround Arjuna and Satyaki, and a great fight follows. Duryodhana reproaches Bhishma for sparing the Pandavas, and Bhishma answers angrily and vows to fight with full force.","kn":"ಕೌರವ ರಾಜರು ಅರ್ಜುನ ಮತ್ತು ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯನ್ನು ಸುತ್ತುವರಿಯುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಮಹಾಯುದ್ಧ ನಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆ. ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಉಳಿಸುತ್ತಿದ್ದಾನೆಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ನಿಂದಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ಪೂರ್ಣಬಲದಿಂದ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಪಣ ತೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कौरव राजा अर्जुन और सात्यकि को घेर लेते हैं और महान युद्ध होता है। दुर्योधन पाण्डवों को बख्शने के लिए भीष्म को फटकारता है, और भीष्म क्रोध से उत्तर देकर पूरी शक्ति से लड़ने का प्रण करते हैं।","te":"కౌరవ రాజులు అర్జునుని, సాత్యకిని చుట్టుముడతారు, మహాయుద్ధం జరుగుతుంది. పాండవులను వదిలేస్తున్నాడని దుర్యోధనుడు భీష్ముని నిందిస్తాడు; భీష్ముడు కోపంతో బదులిచ్చి పూర్తి శక్తితో పోరాడతానని ప్రతిజ్ఞ చేస్తాడు.","ta":"கௌரவ மன்னர்கள் அர்ஜுனனையும் சாத்யகியையும் சூழ, பெரும்போர் நடக்கிறது. பாண்டவரை விட்டுவைப்பதாகத் துரியோதனன் பீஷ்மரைக் கடிந்துகொள்ள, பீஷ்மர் சினந்து பதிலளித்து முழு வலிமையுடன் போரிடுவதாக சபதம் செய்கிறார்.","ml":"കൗരവ രാജാക്കന്മാർ അർജുനനെയും സാത്യകിയെയും വളയുന്നു; ഘോരയുദ്ധം നടക്കുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവരെ വെറുതെവിട്ടതിന് ദുര്യോധനൻ ഭീഷ്മരെ കുറ്റപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മർ കോപത്തോടെ മറുപടി നൽകി പൂർണശക്തിയിൽ യുദ്ധം ചെയ്യുമെന്ന് പ്രതിജ്ഞയെടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.54; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्ते पार्थिवाः क्रुद्धाः फल्गुनं वीक्ष्य संयुगे ।\nरथैरनेकसाहस्रैः समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those angry kings, seeing Phalguna in the battle, surrounded him on all sides with many thousands of chariots."}},{"n":2,"text":"अथैनं रथवृन्देन कोष्टकीकृत्य भारत ।\nशरैः सुबहुसाहस्रैः समन्तादभ्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Making a ring of the mass of chariots around him, O Bharata, they covered him on every side with many thousands of arrows."}},{"n":3,"text":"शक्तीश्च विमलास्तीक्ष्णा गदाश्च परिघैः सह ।\nप्रासान्परश्वधांश्चैव मुद्गरान्मुसलानपि ।\nचिक्षिपुः समरे क्रुद्धाः फल्गुनस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"They hurled bright, sharp spears, maces with iron bars, lances, axes, clubs and pestles at Phalguna's chariot in the fury of battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"शस्त्राणामथ तां वृष्टिं शलभानामिवायतिम् ।\nरुरोध सर्वतः पार्थः शरैः कनकभूषणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Partha, with gold-adorned arrows, stopped from every side that shower of weapons, which came like an approaching swarm of locusts."}},{"n":5,"text":"तत्र तल्लाघवं दृष्ट्वा बीभत्सोरतिमानुषम् ।\nदेवदानवगन्धर्वाः पिशाचोरगराक्षसाः ।\nसाधु साध्विति राजेन्द्र फल्गुनं प्रत्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Bibhatsu's superhuman quickness there, gods, danavas, gandharvas, pishachas, snakes and rakshasas, O king of kings, honored Phalguna, crying \"Well done, well done!\""}},{"n":6,"text":"सात्यकिं चाभिमन्युं च महत्या सेनया सह ।\nगान्धाराः समरे शूरा रुरुधुः सहसौबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The brave Gandharas with Subala's sons held Satyaki and Abhimanyu in battle with a great army."}},{"n":7,"text":"तत्र सौबलकाः क्रुद्धा वार्ष्णेयस्य रथोत्तमम् ।\nतिलशश्चिच्छिदुः क्रोधाच्छस्त्रैर्नानाविधैर्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the angry sons of Subala cut the fine chariot of the Vrishni into sesame-seed pieces with weapons of many kinds in the battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"सात्यकिस्तु रथं त्यक्त्वा वर्तमाने महाभये ।\nअभिमन्यो रथं तूर्णमारुरोह परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, scorcher of foes, leaving his chariot in the great peril, quickly climbed onto Abhimanyu's chariot."}},{"n":9,"text":"तावेकरथसंयुक्तौ सौबलेयस्य वाहिनीम् ।\nव्यधमेतां शितैस्तूर्णं शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sharing one chariot, those two quickly destroyed the army of Subala's son with sharp, straight-jointed arrows."}},{"n":10,"text":"द्रोणभीष्मौ रणे यत्तौ धर्मराजस्य वाहिनीम् ।\nनाशयेतां शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः कङ्कपत्रपरिच्छदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona and Bhishma, both determined, in the battle destroyed the army of the king of dharma with sharp arrows fletched with heron feathers."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो धर्मसुतो राजा माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nमिषतां सर्वसैन्यानां द्रोणानीकमुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, and the two Pandava sons of Madri rushed at Drona's division while all the armies looked on."}},{"n":12,"text":"तत्रासीत्सुमहद्युद्धं तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nयथा देवासुरं युद्धं पूर्वमासीत्सुदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There a great, tumultuous, hair-raising battle took place, as terrible as the ancient fight of gods and asuras."}},{"n":13,"text":"कुर्वाणौ तु महत्कर्म भीमसेनघटोत्कचौ ।\nदुर्योधनस्ततोऽभ्येत्य तावुभावभ्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Bhimasena and Ghatotkacha were doing great deeds, Duryodhana came up and held back both."}},{"n":14,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम हैडिम्बस्य पराक्रमम् ।\nअतीत्य पितरं युद्धे यदयुध्यत भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw the prowess of Hidimba's son, who, surpassing his father, fought in that battle, O Bharata."}},{"n":15,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु संक्रुद्धो दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ।\nहृद्यविध्यत्पृषत्केन प्रहसन्निव पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, enraged, almost laughing, struck the furious Duryodhana in the heart with an arrow."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा प्रहारवरमोहितः ।\nनिषसाद रथोपस्थे कश्मलं च जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, stunned by that excellent blow, sank down on his chariot seat and fainted."}},{"n":17,"text":"तं विसंज्ञमथो ज्ञात्वा त्वरमाणोऽस्य सारथिः ।\nअपोवाह रणाद्राजंस्ततः सैन्यमभिद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing him unconscious, his charioteer hurriedly carried him from the battle, O king, and then his army broke."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततस्तां कौरवीं सेनां द्रवमाणां समन्ततः ।\nनिघ्नन्भीमः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैरनुवव्राज पृष्ठतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima, killing with sharp arrows, followed behind that Kaurava army as it fled in every direction."}},{"n":19,"text":"पार्षतश्च रथश्रेष्ठो धर्मपुत्रश्च पाण्डवः ।\nद्रोणस्य पश्यतः सैन्यं गाङ्गेयस्य च पश्यतः ।\nजघ्नतुर्विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैः परानीकविशातनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchala prince, best of chariot-warriors, and Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, struck down that army before Drona's and Ganga's son's very eyes, with sharp arrows that scatter the enemy force."}},{"n":20,"text":"द्रवमाणं तु तत्सैन्यं तव पुत्रस्य संयुगे ।\nनाशक्नुतां वारयितुं भीष्मद्रोणौ महारथौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma and Drona, great chariot-warriors, could not stop that army of your son as it fled in the battle."}},{"n":21,"text":"वार्यमाणं हि भीष्मेण द्रोणेन च विशां पते ।\nविद्रवत्येव तत्सैन्यं पश्यतोर्द्रोणभीष्मयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though held back by Bhishma and Drona, lord of the people, that army fled on while Drona and Bhishma looked on."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो रथसहस्रेषु विद्रवत्सु ततस्ततः ।\nतावास्थितावेकरथं सौभद्रशिनिपुंगवौ ।\nसौबलीं समरे सेनां शातयेतां समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as thousands of chariots fled in every direction, Subhadra's son and the bull of the Shinis, standing on one chariot, shattered Subala's son's army on every side."}},{"n":23,"text":"शुशुभाते तदा तौ तु शैनेयकुरुपुंगवौ ।\nअमावास्यां गतौ यद्वत्सोमसूर्यौ नभस्तले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two, the Shini warrior and the bull of the Kurus, shone then like the moon and sun in the sky on the new-moon day."}},{"n":24,"text":"अर्जुनस्तु ततः क्रुद्धस्तव सैन्यं विशां पते ।\nववर्ष शरवर्षेण धाराभिरिव तोयदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, in a fury, rained showers of arrows on your army, lord of the people, as a cloud rains in torrents."}},{"n":25,"text":"वध्यमानं ततस्तत्तु शरैः पार्थस्य संयुगे ।\nदुद्राव कौरवं सैन्यं विषादभयकम्पितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by Partha's arrows in the battle, the Kaurava army fled, trembling with dismay and fear."}},{"n":26,"text":"द्रवतस्तान्समालोक्य भीष्मद्रोणौ महारथौ ।\nन्यवारयेतां संरब्धौ दुर्योधनहितैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them flee, the great chariot-warriors Bhishma and Drona, wishing Duryodhana well, angrily tried to stop them."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा समाश्वस्य विशां पते ।\nन्यवर्तयत तत्सैन्यं द्रवमाणं समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, having recovered, lord of the people, turned back his army that was fleeing in all directions."}},{"n":28,"text":"यत्र यत्र सुतं तुभ्यं यो यः पश्यति भारत ।\nतत्र तत्र न्यवर्तन्त क्षत्रियाणां महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever any of them saw your son, there the great chariot-warriors of the kshatriyas turned back, O Bharata."}},{"n":29,"text":"तान्निवृत्तान्समीक्ष्यैव ततोऽन्येऽपीतरे जनाः ।\nअन्योन्यस्पर्धया राजँल्लज्जयान्येऽवतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them turned back, the others too, out of rivalry with one another and shame, stood their ground, O king."}},{"n":30,"text":"पुनरावर्ततां तेषां वेग आसीद्विशां पते ।\nपूर्यतः सागरस्येव चन्द्रस्योदयनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rush of those turning back, lord of the people, was like the swelling of the sea toward the rising of the moon."}},{"n":31,"text":"संनिवृत्तांस्ततस्तांस्तु दृष्ट्वा राजा सुयोधनः ।\nअब्रवीत्त्वरितो गत्वा भीष्मं शांतनवं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them rallied, King Suyodhana quickly went to Bhishma, son of Shantanu, and spoke these words."}},{"n":32,"text":"पितामह निबोधेदं यत्त्वा वक्ष्यामि भारत ।\nनानुरूपमहं मन्ये त्वयि जीवति कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Grandfather, hear what I tell you, O Bharata. I think it is not fitting, Kaurava, while you live,\""}},{"n":33,"text":"द्रोणे चास्त्रविदां श्रेष्ठे सपुत्रे ससुहृज्जने ।\nकृपे चैव महेष्वासे द्रवतीयं वरूथिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"and Drona lives, best of those who know weapons, with his son and friends, and the great archer Kripa, that this army of ours should flee.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"न पाण्डवाः प्रतिबलास्तव राजन्कथंचन ।\nतथा द्रोणस्य संग्रामे द्रौणेश्चैव कृपस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Pandavas are in no way a match for you, O king, nor for Drona in battle, nor for Drona's son, nor for Kripa.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"अनुग्राह्याः पाण्डुसुता नूनं तव पितामह ।\nयथेमां क्षमसे वीर वध्यमानां वरूथिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely, grandfather, you have a soft spot for the sons of Pandu, since you tolerate this army of ours being slaughtered, hero.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"सोऽस्मि वाच्यस्त्वया राजन्पूर्वमेव समागमे ।\nन योत्स्ये पाण्डवान्संख्ये नापि पार्षतसात्यकी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You should have told me so at our first meeting, O king: 'I will not fight the Pandavas in battle, nor Prishata's son, nor Satyaki.'\""}},{"n":37,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु वचनं तुभ्यमाचार्यस्य कृपस्य च ।\nकर्णेन सहितः कृत्यं चिन्तयानस्तदैव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing your words and those of the teacher and Kripa, I would have considered with Karna what had to be done then.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"यदि नाहं परित्याज्यो युवाभ्यामिह संयुगे ।\nविक्रमेणानुरूपेण युध्येतां पुरुषर्षभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I am not to be given up by you two here in battle, fight, you two bulls among men, with valor worthy of yourselves.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा वचो भीष्मः प्रहसन्वै मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nअब्रवीत्तनयं तुभ्यं क्रोधादुद्वृत्य चक्षुषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing these words, Bhishma, laughing again and again, spoke to your son, his eyes rolling up in anger."}},{"n":40,"text":"बहुशो हि मया राजंस्तथ्यमुक्तं हितं वचः ।\nअजेयाः पाण्डवा युद्धे देवैरपि सवासवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Many times, king, I have told you true and helpful words: the Pandavas cannot be conquered in battle even by the gods with Indra.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"यत्तु शक्यं मया कर्तुं वृद्धेनाद्य नृपोत्तम ।\nकरिष्यामि यथाशक्ति प्रेक्षेदानीं सबान्धवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But what I can do today, best of kings, old as I am, I shall do to the best of my strength. Watch now, with your kinsmen.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"अद्य पाण्डुसुतान्सर्वान्ससैन्यान्सह बन्धुभिः ।\nमिषतो वारयिष्यामि सर्वलोकस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, before the eyes of all the world, I shall hold back all the sons of Pandu with their army and their kin.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"एवमुक्ते तु भीष्मेण पुत्रास्तव जनेश्वर ।\nदध्मुः शङ्खान्मुदा युक्ता भेरीश्च जघ्निरे भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhishma had said this, your sons, lord of men, joyfully blew their conches and struck their drums loudly."}},{"n":44,"text":"पाण्डवापि ततो राजञ्श्रुत्वा तं निनदं महत् ।\nदध्मुः शङ्खांश्च भेरीश्च मुरजांश्च व्यनादयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandavas too, hearing that great sound, blew their conches and drums and made the muravas resound."}}]}]}